be does observe a completed transfer, so the outcome is a wrong success report and a leadership interruption rather than a cluster that never recovers.\\\"\n]\n\ntransfer_interp['limitations']=[\n \\\"Whether the call reports success and the target cannot win is established by one execution per case (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, indices 0-3); the identity of the leader after the interruption is timing dependent and is only recorded, not asserted.\\\",\n \\\"The leaderless interval is not bounded by this receipt: leadership state was sampled once after the returned result and after a 1500ms wait, so no interval measurement exists yet; the revised probe with 1ms sampling is submitted for that.\\\",\n \\\"The claim concerns the reported result of the call, the requested target's inability to win and the observed leadership change; it does not assert data loss, since committed entries remain committed and a fresh election follows.\\\",\n \\\"The probe uses one process with real Raft instances and in-memory transports, so it exercises the leader's own transfer, election and vote paths but not process-level partitions or multi-host clocks.\\\"\n]\n\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed transfer probe for @transfer_nonvoter against its question: the call naming a non-voter reports success while the requested server never becomes leader and leadership moves to another term (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, parsed indices 0-3), with the voter-target control completing a real transfer. The account is now execution-backed and the question's liveness half is recorded as partial: that receipt sampled leadership only at endpoints, so a revised probe was built which samples leadership every millisecond, records leaderless sample counts and the first and last leaderless millisecond, and asserts that the previous leader was observed outside Leader state and that the cluster was observed with no leader at all. Its execution is requested as a revision of the same experiment. This update also answers both registered gaps with the partial progress available: for @verify_quorum no successor-overlap condition has been identified, and for @transfer_nonvoter the interruption is shown to happen but its length is still unmeasured.\\\")\n\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous run of this harness answered the reported-result half of the question but sampled leadership state only at endpoints, so it could not say whether the cluster was ever without a leader or how long that lasted. This revision adds a 1ms sampling goroutine that runs from the transfer call until after the observation window and reports leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, how often the previous leader was seen outside Leader state, and the endpoint leader identity, plus two comparisons asserting those observations for the non-voter case. Measured result fields are unchanged and no case, partition or target-selection logic changed.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe both halves of a leadership transfer request naming a non-voter: what LeadershipTransferToServer reports, which server actually holds leadership, and how the cluster's leadership state evolves during the attempt, sampled every millisecond, with the same call naming a voter as the control. Each case emits an assurance_transfer_target setup event and an assurance_transfer_result event carrying the returned result, target and previous-leader states, leader sets and terms, and the sampling counters described above.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Three voters plus one non-voter is a supported configuration; the non-voter is joined through the leader's own AddNonvoter call.\\\",\n   \\\"HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms and CommitTimeout = 5ms satisfy Config.Validate, and protocol version >= 3 supports LeadershipTransferToServer.\\\",\n   \\\"A voter target is a legal and expected use, so the voter case is the control that the probe can observe a completed transfer.\\\",\n   \\\"Sampling every millisecond with in-memory transports is fine-grained relative to the 200ms election timeout, so a leaderless interval that lasts an election round is expected to be visible; shorter gaps are not bounded by this sampling rate.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\n   \\\"Process-level stalls, host suspends and multi-host clock behaviour, which the single-process in-memory probe does not reproduce.\\\"\n  ]\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case builds four real Raft instances in one process with their own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, fully connected before any node starts. Three voters are bootstrapped with BootstrapCluster as Voter; the fourth node is started without a configuration and joined through the elected leader's own AddNonvoter(id, address, 0, 5s) call, waiting until the leader's latest configuration reports it. \\\"\n  \\\"The target is chosen by configuration role, never by a measured result: the first voter that is not the leader as the control, the joined non-voter as the probe; its suffrage is read from the leader's latest configuration and emitted in the setup event. The case then calls leader.LeadershipTransferToServer(target.id, target.addr) and, from the instant of that call, a goroutine samples every millisecond: whether any of the four nodes is in Leader state, and whether the previous leader is outside Leader state. It waits up to 5s for the returned result, up to 1500ms for the requested target to be observed as Leader, and then records the leader set, the maximum term, whether the term rose above the pre-call term, and the sampling counters. Both cases share the harness TestAssuranceLeadershipTransferTarget under distinct case names.\\\"),\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_target\\\"}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: what the call reported. Holds means the predicted success report was observed, which supports the defect account rather than contradicting it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the requested server never became leader within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"old_leader_lost_leadership_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the previous leader was sampled outside Leader state during the attempt, so it did give up leadership.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leaderless_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: at least one sample found no leader in the cluster, with the first and last leaderless millisecond recorded alongside.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the same call does transfer leadership, so the non-voter outcome is not a probe that never transfers.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the reported result for a transfer that does complete.\\\"}\n ]\n}\n\nfor key in ('sources','knowledge','gaps','investigations'):\n    d.pop(key,None)\njson.dump(d, open('update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"  File \"<stdin>\", line 15\n    \"resolved\": False}})\n                       ^\nSyntaxError: closing parenthesis ')' does not match opening parenthesis '{' on line 10\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"2190c36cecef4055bdfd7441367c6e18\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 664.5484418269989, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"unchanged\", \"targets\": [\"verify_leader\", \"quorum_size\", \"lease_check\", \"start_stop_repl\", \"follower_vote_grant\", \"notify_all\", \"update_last_appended\", \"heartbeat_ack\", \"install_snapshot_ack\", \"verify_vote\", \"api_verify_leader\", \"config_validation\", \"reload_config\", \"timeout_now\", \"candidate_skips_prevote\", \"vote_term_bump\", \"transfer_target_lookup\", \"transfer_lost_leadership\", \"pick_server_voters\", \"api_transfer_to_server\", \"docs_transfer\"]}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"unchanged\", \"targets\": [\"@verify_counts_nonvoter\", \"@lease_voter_only\", \"@reload_keeps_lease_bounds\", \"@transfer_accepts_nonvoter\"]}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"unchanged\", \"targets\": [\"@verify_quorum\", \"@transfer_nonvoter\"]}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"unchanged\", \"targets\": [\"@verify_quorum\", \"@transfer_nonvoter\"]}, {\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nvi,ti=d['interpretations'][0],d['interpretations'][1]\nvi['answers']={\\\"d704b04e706144dc964ff451359eda19-gap-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Partial progress only. The receipt for this question did not witness a successor being elected while the old leader verified: in the non-voter partition the other servers stayed in term 2 with no leader change and the leader was still Leader at the endpoint. The two configuration routes that could stretch the old leader's mandate past a follower's election timer are closed by source: checkLeaderLease counts voters only, and ReloadConfig re-runs ValidateConfig so LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout holds on a running node. What remains to be shown is a leader-side timing condition - a stall or clock jump longer than ElectionTimeout minus LeaderLeaseTimeout, or a verify request admitted before the ready lease case - and no legal instance has been identified.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}\nti['conclusion']=\\\"explained\\\"\nti['executions']={\\\"b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd\\\":[0,1,2,3]}\nti['answers']={\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-gap-1\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Partial progress. The execution shows the previous leader does not keep leadership: in the non-voter case it was not Leader at the endpoint and the cluster's maximum term had risen from 2 to 4 with the same server holding leadership at term 4, which a leader cannot do without having stepped down and won a later election. The leaderless interval itself is not bounded by that receipt, because leadership was only sampled when the returned result and the 1500ms target window ended. The revised probe submitted here samples leadership every millisecond and records leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, and how often the previous leader was seen outside Leader state.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}\nti['rationale']=(\\\"The question was whether LeadershipTransferToServer reports a transfer that the named server can complete when that server is a non-voter, and what happens to leadership while it cannot. The execution answers the first half directly. In the control case naming a voter (parsed indices 0 and 1) the call returned nil and the requested server was Leader at the endpoint while the previous leader was Follower, so the call does perform real transfers. In the case naming the non-voter (parsed indices 2 and 3, setup event index 2 matched as admission) the same call returned nil while the requested server was never observed as Leader within 1500ms and finished as Follower; the previous leader was not Leader at the endpoint and the maximum term across the cluster had risen from 2 to 4, with the same server holding leadership at term 4, which a Raft leader cannot do without having stepped down and won a later election. \\\"\n \\\"The source explains the mechanism as predicted. The leader resolves the requested ID only through leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication populates for every configured server except the leader without consulting Suffrage, so a non-voter passes and receives TimeoutNow; timeoutNow sets it to Candidate and marks candidateFromLeadershipTransfer, a flag that by design suppresses pre-vote, so it sends a real RequestVote carrying the next term. Each voter adopts the higher term and becomes a follower before reaching the hasVote check, which then refuses the vote because the candidate holds no vote, so the requested server can never collect a grant. The old leader learns of the higher term, steps down, and its transfer goroutine reports success from the leftLeaderLoop branch, so the caller is told the transfer succeeded while leadership has in fact left it for a server it did not choose, or returned to it in a later term. \\\"\n \\\"That mismatch is the defect: for the documented purpose of handing leadership over, a success result that the named target can never satisfy leaves the caller unable to distinguish a completed handover from a self-inflicted leadership interruption. The liveness side is bounded rather than unbounded and this receipt does not measure it, since leadership was sampled only at the end of the observation window; the revised probe samples every millisecond and records the leaderless samples. No data loss is claimed: committed entries stay committed and a voter is elected afterwards.\\\")\nti['counterevidence']=[\n \\\"The API comment does not state that the target must be a voter, and a caller who names only voters never reaches this path, so the defect depends on an accepted calling pattern rather than on the library's own choice of target.\\\",\n \\\"LeadershipTransfer() without an explicit target filters non-voters in pickServer, which shows the intended transfer target set is the voter set and supports reading the targeted call as requiring the same premise.\\\",\n \\\"A TimeoutNow that cannot be delivered (unreachable target) is reported as an error by the transfer path, so not every unusable target is silently accepted.\\\",\n \\\"The interruption is bounded: the remaining voters re-elect after their election timers, and the control case shows the probe does observe a completed transfer, so the outcome is a wrong success report and a leadership interruption rather than a cluster that never recovers.\\\"]\nti['limitations']=[\n \\\"Whether the call reports success and the requested target cannot win rests on one execution per case (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, indices 0-3); the identity of the leader after the interruption is timing dependent and is only recorded, not asserted.\\\",\n \\\"The leaderless interval is not bounded by this receipt: leadership state was sampled once after the returned result and after a 1500ms wait, so no interval measurement exists yet; the revised probe with 1ms sampling is submitted for that.\\\",\n \\\"The claim concerns the reported result of the call, the requested target's inability to win and the observed leadership change; it does not assert data loss.\\\",\n \\\"The probe uses one process with real Raft instances and in-memory transports, so it exercises the leader's own transfer, election and vote paths but not process-level partitions or multi-host clocks.\\\"]\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed transfer probe for @transfer_nonvoter against its question: the call naming a non-voter reports success while the requested server never becomes leader and leadership moves to a later term (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, parsed indices 0-3), with the voter-target control completing a real transfer. The account is now execution-backed, and the question's liveness half is recorded as partial because that receipt sampled leadership only at endpoints; a revised probe was built that samples every millisecond, records leaderless sample counts and the first and last leaderless millisecond, and asserts both that the previous leader was observed outside Leader state and that the cluster was observed with no leader at all. Its execution is requested as a revision of the same experiment. This update also answers both registered gaps with the partial progress available: no successor-overlap condition has been identified for @verify_quorum, and for @transfer_nonvoter the interruption is shown to occur but its length is still unmeasured.\\\")\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous run of this harness answered the reported-result half of the question but sampled leadership state only at endpoints, so it could not say whether the cluster was ever without a leader or for how long. This revision adds a 1ms sampling goroutine running from the transfer call until after the observation window, reporting leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, how often the previous leader was seen outside Leader state, and the endpoint leader identity, with two comparisons asserting those observations for the non-voter case. Measured result fields, cases and target selection are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe both halves of a leadership transfer request naming a non-voter: what LeadershipTransferToServer reports, which server actually holds leadership, and how the cluster's leadership state evolves during the attempt, sampled every millisecond, with the same call naming a voter as the control. Each case emits an assurance_transfer_target setup event and an assurance_transfer_result event carrying the returned result, the target and previous-leader states, leader sets and terms, and the sampling counters.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Three voters plus one non-voter is a supported configuration; the non-voter is joined through the leader's own AddNonvoter call.\\\",\\\"HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms and CommitTimeout = 5ms satisfy Config.Validate, and protocol version >= 3 supports LeadershipTransferToServer.\\\",\\\"A voter target is a legal and expected use, so the voter case is the control that the probe can observe a completed transfer.\\\",\\\"Sampling every millisecond is fine-grained relative to the 200ms election timeout, so a leaderless interval lasting an election round is expected to be visible; shorter gaps are not bounded by this sampling rate.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Process-level stalls, host suspends and multi-host clock behaviour, which a single-process in-memory probe does not reproduce.\\\"]},\n \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case builds four real Raft instances in one process with their own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, fully connected before any node starts. Three voters are bootstrapped with BootstrapCluster as Voter; the fourth node is started without a configuration and joined through the elected leader's own AddNonvoter(id, address, 0, 5s) call, waiting until the leader's latest configuration reports it. \\\"\n  \\\"The target is chosen by configuration role, never by a measured result: the first voter that is not the leader as the control, the joined non-voter as the probe; its suffrage is read from the leader's latest configuration and emitted in the setup event. The case calls leader.LeadershipTransferToServer(target.id, target.addr) and, from that instant, a goroutine samples every millisecond whether any of the four nodes is in Leader state and whether the previous leader is outside Leader state. It waits up to 5s for the returned result, up to 1500ms for the requested target to be observed as Leader, then records the leader set, the maximum term, whether the term rose above the pre-call term, and the sampling counters. Both cases share the harness TestAssuranceLeadershipTransferTarget under distinct case names.\\\"),\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_target\\\"}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: what the call reported. Holds means the predicted success report was observed, which supports the defect account rather than contradicting it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the requested server never became leader within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"old_leader_lost_leadership_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the previous leader was sampled outside Leader state during the attempt, so it did give up leadership.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leaderless_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: at least one sample found no leader in the cluster, with the first and last leaderless millisecond recorded alongside.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the same call does transfer leadership, so the non-voter outcome is not a probe that never transfers.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the reported result for a transfer that does complete.\\\"}]}\nfor k in ('sources','knowledge','gaps','investigations'): d.pop(k,None)\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nvi,ti=d['interpretations'][0],d['interpretations'][1]\nvi['answers']={\\\"d704b04e706144dc964ff451359eda19-gap-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Partial progress only. The receipt for this question did not witness a successor being elected while the old leader verified: in the non-voter partition the other servers stayed in term 2 with no leader change and the leader was still Leader at the endpoint. The two configuration routes that could stretch the old leader's mandate past a follower's election timer are closed by source: checkLeaderLease counts voters only, and ReloadConfig re-runs ValidateConfig so LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout holds on a running node. What remains to be shown is a leader-side timing condition - a stall or clock jump longer than ElectionTimeout minus LeaderLeaseTimeout, or a verify request admitted before the ready lease case - and no legal instance has been identified.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}\nti['conclusion']=\\\"explained\\\"\nti['executions']={\\\"b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd\\\":[0,1,2,3]}\nti['answers']={\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-gap-1\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Partial progress. The execution shows the previous leader does not keep leadership: in the non-voter case it was not Leader at the endpoint and the cluster's maximum term had risen from 2 to 4 with the same server holding leadership at term 4, which a leader cannot do without having stepped down and won a later election. The leaderless interval itself is not bounded by that receipt, because leadership was only sampled when the returned result and the 1500ms target window ended. The revised probe submitted here samples leadership every millisecond and records leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, and how often the previous leader was seen outside Leader state.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}\nti['rationale']=(\\\"The question was whether LeadershipTransferToServer reports a transfer that the named server can complete when that server is a non-voter, and what happens to leadership while it cannot. The execution answers the first half directly. In the control case naming a voter (parsed indices 0 and 1) the call returned nil and the requested server was Leader at the endpoint while the previous leader was Follower, so the call does perform real transfers. In the case naming the non-voter (parsed indices 2 and 3, setup event index 2 matched as admission) the same call returned nil while the requested server was never observed as Leader within 1500ms and finished as Follower; the previous leader was not Leader at the endpoint and the maximum term across the cluster had risen from 2 to 4, with the same server holding leadership at term 4, which a Raft leader cannot do without having stepped down and won a later election. \\\"\n \\\"The source explains the mechanism as predicted. The leader resolves the requested ID only through leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication populates for every configured server except the leader without consulting Suffrage, so a non-voter passes and receives TimeoutNow; timeoutNow sets it to Candidate and marks candidateFromLeadershipTransfer, a flag that by design suppresses pre-vote, so it sends a real RequestVote carrying the next term. Each voter adopts the higher term and becomes a follower before reaching the hasVote check, which then refuses the vote because the candidate holds no vote, so the requested server can never collect a grant. The old leader learns of the higher term, steps down, and its transfer goroutine reports success from the leftLeaderLoop branch, so the caller is told the transfer succeeded while leadership has in fact left it for a server it did not choose, or returned to it in a later term. \\\"\n \\\"That mismatch is the defect: for the documented purpose of handing leadership over, a success result that the named target can never satisfy leaves the caller unable to distinguish a completed handover from a self-inflicted leadership interruption. The liveness side is bounded rather than unbounded and this receipt does not measure it, since leadership was sampled only at the end of the observation window; the revised probe samples every millisecond and records the leaderless samples. No data loss is claimed: committed entries stay committed and a voter is elected afterwards.\\\")\nti['counterevidence']=[\n \\\"The API comment does not state that the target must be a voter, and a caller who names only voters never reaches this path, so the defect depends on an accepted calling pattern rather than on the library's own choice of target.\\\",\n \\\"LeadershipTransfer() without an explicit target filters non-voters in pickServer, which shows the intended transfer target set is the voter set and supports reading the targeted call as requiring the same premise.\\\",\n \\\"A TimeoutNow that cannot be delivered (unreachable target) is reported as an error by the transfer path, so not every unusable target is silently accepted.\\\",\n \\\"The interruption is bounded: the remaining voters re-elect after their election timers, and the control case shows the probe does observe a completed transfer, so the outcome is a wrong success report and a leadership interruption rather than a cluster that never recovers.\\\"]\nti['limitations']=[\n \\\"Whether the call reports success and the requested target cannot win rests on one execution per case (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, indices 0-3); the identity of the leader after the interruption is timing dependent and is only recorded, not asserted.\\\",\n \\\"The leaderless interval is not bounded by this receipt: leadership state was sampled once after the returned result and after a 1500ms wait, so no interval measurement exists yet; the revised probe with 1ms sampling is submitted for that.\\\",\n \\\"The claim concerns the reported result of the call, the requested target's inability to win and the observed leadership change; it does not assert data loss.\\\",\n \\\"The probe uses one process with real Raft instances and in-memory transports, so it exercises the leader's own transfer, election and vote paths but not process-level partitions or multi-host clocks.\\\"]\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed transfer probe for @transfer_nonvoter against its question: the call naming a non-voter reports success while the requested server never becomes leader and leadership moves to a later term (receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, parsed indices 0-3), with the voter-target control completing a real transfer. The account is now execution-backed, and the question's liveness half is recorded as partial because that receipt sampled leadership only at endpoints; a revised probe was built that samples every millisecond, records leaderless sample counts and the first and last leaderless millisecond, and asserts both that the previous leader was observed outside Leader state and that the cluster was observed with no leader at all. Its execution is requested as a revision of the same experiment. This update also answers both registered gaps with the partial progress available: no successor-overlap condition has been identified for @verify_quorum, and for @transfer_nonvoter the interruption is shown to occur but its length is still unmeasured.\\\")\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The previous run of this harness answered the reported-result half of the question but sampled leadership state only at endpoints, so it could not say whether the cluster was ever without a leader or for how long. This revision adds a 1ms sampling goroutine running from the transfer call until after the observation window, reporting leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, how often the previous leader was seen outside Leader state, and the endpoint leader identity, with two comparisons asserting those observations for the non-voter case. Measured result fields, cases and target selection are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_transfer_to_server\\\",\\\"transfer_target_lookup\\\",\\\"timeout_now\\\",\\\"candidate_skips_prevote\\\",\\\"vote_term_bump\\\",\\\"transfer_lost_leadership\\\",\\\"pick_server_voters\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe both halves of a leadership transfer request naming a non-voter: what LeadershipTransferToServer reports, which server actually holds leadership, and how the cluster's leadership state evolves during the attempt, sampled every millisecond, with the same call naming a voter as the control. Each case emits an assurance_transfer_target setup event and an assurance_transfer_result event carrying the returned result, the target and previous-leader states, leader sets and terms, and the sampling counters.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Three voters plus one non-voter is a supported configuration; the non-voter is joined through the leader's own AddNonvoter call.\\\",\\\"HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms and CommitTimeout = 5ms satisfy Config.Validate, and protocol version >= 3 supports LeadershipTransferToServer.\\\",\\\"A voter target is a legal and expected use, so the voter case is the control that the probe can observe a completed transfer.\\\",\\\"Sampling every millisecond is fine-grained relative to the 200ms election timeout, so a leaderless interval lasting an election round is expected to be visible; shorter gaps are not bounded by this sampling rate.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Process-level stalls, host suspends and multi-host clock behaviour, which a single-process in-memory probe does not reproduce.\\\"]},\n \\\"prefix\\\":(\\\"Each case builds four real Raft instances in one process with their own InmemStore, InmemSnapshotStore and InmemTransport, fully connected before any node starts. Three voters are bootstrapped with BootstrapCluster as Voter; the fourth node is started without a configuration and joined through the elected leader's own AddNonvoter(id, address, 0, 5s) call, waiting until the leader's latest configuration reports it. \\\"\n  \\\"The target is chosen by configuration role, never by a measured result: the first voter that is not the leader as the control, the joined non-voter as the probe; its suffrage is read from the leader's latest configuration and emitted in the setup event. The case calls leader.LeadershipTransferToServer(target.id, target.addr) and, from that instant, a goroutine samples every millisecond whether any of the four nodes is in Leader state and whether the previous leader is outside Leader state. It waits up to 5s for the returned result, up to 1500ms for the requested target to be observed as Leader, then records the leader set, the maximum term, whether the term rose above the pre-call term, and the sampling counters. Both cases share the harness TestAssuranceLeadershipTransferTarget under distinct case names.\\\"),\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_target\\\"}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: what the call reported. Holds means the predicted success report was observed, which supports the defect account rather than contradicting it.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the requested server never became leader within the observation window.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"old_leader_lost_leadership_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: the previous leader was sampled outside Leader state during the attempt, so it did give up leadership.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leaderless_observed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Nonvoter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Non-voter target: at least one sample found no leader in the cluster, with the first and last leaderless millisecond recorded alongside.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the same call does transfer leadership, so the non-voter outcome is not a probe that never transfers.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance_transfer_result\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\",\\\"leader_id\\\",\\\"target_id\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"attempt\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"transfer_error\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"nil\\\"},\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"target_suffrage\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Voter\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Voter target control: the reported result for a transfer that does complete.\\\"}]}\nfor k in ('sources','knowledge','gaps','investigations'): d.pop(k,None)\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"2190c36cecef4055bdfd7441367c6e18\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 664.5484418269989, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"submission\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Unknown local batch reference: @verify_quorum\", \"allowed\": []}], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
