{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the transfer receipt (b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd, parsed indices 0-3): naming a voter, the call returned nil and the requested server ended as Leader with the previous leader Follower; naming the non-voter, the same call returned nil while the requested server was never Leader in a 1500ms window, finished Follower, and the cluster's maximum term rose 2 to 4 with the same server leading at term 4 — so the handover reported as successful never reached the named target. The question account is now 'explained' with the source mechanism (target resolved through replState, TimeoutNow, pre-vote skipped, voters adopting the higher term then rejecting the vote, old leader's goroutine reporting success from leftLeaderLoop). Both registered gaps are now answered with partial progress and left unresolved, and I revised the probe to bound the liveness half: a 1ms sampling goroutine records leaderless sample counts, the first and last leaderless millisecond, and how often the previous leader was outside Leader state, with two new comparisons asserting those observations; its execution is requested as a revision of the same experiment. Unfinished: citing that receipt, the liveness interval bound, and any follow-up on why the target selection admits non-voters.\"}"}}
